public class PinCheck {
    // true only for exactly four ASCII digits '0'-'9'
    static boolean isValidPin(String s) {
        if (s == null || s.length() != 4) return false;
        for (int i = 0; i < 4; i++) {
            char c = s.charAt(i);
            if (c < '0' || c > '9') return false;
        }
        return true;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String[] input = {"1234", "0000", "9999", "123", "12345", "", "12a4",
                          " 123", "12.3", "-123", "\u09E7\u09E8\u09E9\u09EA", null};
        boolean[] expected = {true, true, true, false, false, false, false,
                              false, false, false, false, false};
        int pass = 0;
        for (int i = 0; i < input.length; i++) {
            boolean got = isValidPin(input[i]);
            boolean ok = (got == expected[i]);
            if (ok) pass++;
            System.out.println("TC" + (i + 1) + " -> " + got + (ok ? " PASS" : " FAIL"));
        }
        System.out.println(pass + "/" + input.length + " passed");
    }
}

Output (compiled and run with javac/java):
TC1 -> true PASS
TC2 -> true PASS
TC3 -> true PASS
TC4 -> false PASS
TC5 -> false PASS
TC6 -> false PASS
TC7 -> false PASS
TC8 -> false PASS
TC9 -> false PASS
TC10 -> false PASS
TC11 -> false PASS
TC12 -> false PASS
12/12 passed

Test design
| TC | Input | Class / boundary | Expected |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1–3 | 1234, 0000, 9999 | valid class; lowest and highest values | true |
| 4, 5 | 123, 12345 | length 3 and 5 (boundary ± 1) | false |
| 6 | "" | empty | false |
| 7–10 | 12a4, " 123", 12.3, -123 | letter, space, symbol, sign | false |
| 11 | ১২৩৪ | Bangla digits | false |
| 12 | null | missing value | false |

Why not Character.isDigit(): it returns true for any Unicode decimal digit, including Bangla ১ (U+09E7), so "১২৩৪" would pass. The PIN is later compared or hashed as ASCII, so the check must be the explicit range '0' to '9'.

The method keeps the string (not an int) so leading zeros such as 0000 survive, and it never throws on null.

